  "unresolved": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "f1-chained-gate-missed",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "criterion": "spec-31-1",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/queue-check.mjs:262",
      "assumption": "Spec 31 adds a spaced & only; shell chaining is not in its list.",
      "summary": "Missed in every version (base and HEAD): \"Check: pnpm verify && pnpm lint pass.\", \"pnpm verify | tee gate.log passes.\" and \"pnpm verify 2>&1 | tee log.\". Each runs the gate. Under the brief's cost rule a miss is the costly error. A fix: let `&&`, `||`, `|` and `2>&1` followed by whitespace end the command (receipt review-31-hunt-names.log)."
    },
    {
      "id": "f2-number-and-hyphen-words-read-as-prose",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "criterion": "spec-31-2",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/queue-check.mjs:261-262",
      "assumption": "The implementer's flagged edge is accepted: the spec requires \"2 times\" and \"re-runs\" to name the gate, and the brief says a missed gate costs more than a false gap.",
      "summary": "Judged against the cost rule, the edge is acceptable. \"pnpm test 2 passes\" is newly true; \"pnpm test—run passes\" was already true at base 3c695f9~1, so it is not new. Because a prose word now takes inner hyphens, \"pnpm test button-group passes.\" and \"yarn test date-utils passes.\" (Jest/Vitest file filters) are newly true too. All of these are false gaps, the cheaper error, and a spec author can quote the command in a code span to clear them. The doc comment at queue-check.mjs:231 still says a next word holding `-` does not name the gate. It should say an inner hyphen between letters reads as prose (receipt review-31-hunt-names.log)."
    },
    {
      "id": "f3-probe-receipts-need-gate-at-archive",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "criterion": "spec-31-3",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/references/delivery.md:53",
      "assumption": "The spec names probe.mjs as a file that needs the gate, so the refusal is intended.",
      "summary": "This feature folder holds 38 reviewer probe receipts with source extensions (spec-01-probe.mjs ... spec-23-probe.mjs, spec-09-footer.sh, spec-21-walk.sh). When session end archives the feature after the gate, the push now refuses with gate-receipt-stale and the gate must run again (hunt case \"archive move of a folder holding a probe .mjs receipt\"). delivery.md:53 says only \"a record in a feature or archive folder\" and does not list the extensions. Reviewer guidance does not say to save probes as .mjs.txt either. A fix: list the record extensions in delivery.md, and tell reviewers to save probe scripts with a .txt suffix. This feature then costs one extra gate run at archive, or its probes are renamed first."
    }
  ],
